<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Home on PageMailer</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/</link><description>Recent content in Home on PageMailer</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://pagemailer.app/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Installation</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/install/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/install/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="prerequisites">Prerequisites&lt;/h2>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Ensure you are using Confluence Cloud, as PageMailer does not support server instances.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h2 id="installation-steps">Installation Steps&lt;/h2>
&lt;h3 id="1-go-to-the-atlassian-marketplace">1. Go to the Atlassian Marketplace&lt;/h3>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>
&lt;p>Visit the &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/go/marketplace">PageMailer app listing on Atlassian Marketplace&lt;/a>.
&lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/install-from-marketplace.png" target="_blank" class="flex flex-col items-start">
 &lt;img src="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/install-from-marketplace.png" alt="Installing from the Atlassian Marketplace" title="Installing from the Atlassian Marketplace"class="max-h-80 max-w-[min(100%,36rem)] !mb-0 !mt-0 !rounded-md"
 >
 &lt;/a>&lt;/p>
&lt;/li>
&lt;li>
&lt;p>Or directly from Confluence:
&lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/install-from-confluence.png" target="_blank" class="flex flex-col items-start">
 &lt;img src="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/install-from-confluence.png" alt="Installing from Confluence" title="Installing from Confluence"class="max-h-80 max-w-[min(100%,36rem)] !mb-0 !mt-0 !rounded-md"
 >
 &lt;/a>&lt;/p>
&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h3 id="2-install-the-app">2. Install the app&lt;/h3>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Click &lt;strong>Install&lt;/strong> or &lt;strong>Try it free&lt;/strong>.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Authorize required permissions, such as:
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Get Confluence page list and content&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Access user profile (used for user mentions in pages)&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h3 id="3-verify-the-installation">3. Verify the installation&lt;/h3>
&lt;p>To ensure PageMailer was successfully installed, try to visit the app&amp;rsquo;s &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/">settings&lt;/a> page,
and make sure you are able to &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/basic-usage/send-an-email/">send an email&lt;/a>.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Logos &amp; Socials</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/logos-socials/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/logos-socials/</guid><description>&lt;p>Logos &amp;amp; Socials settings are accessible as a tab on PageMailer&amp;rsquo;s settings page. &lt;em>You can find the app&amp;rsquo;s settings by following &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/">this step-by-step guide&lt;/a>.&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="social-media-links">Social media links&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>You can optionally set up social media links that can be displayed in the footer of your email communications. This is an option that can be turned on or off on a per-template basis, and you can find out more about how to use it in the &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/templates/">template settings&lt;/a>.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Templates</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/templates/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/templates/</guid><description>&lt;p>Template management is accessible as a tab on PageMailer&amp;rsquo;s settings page. &lt;em>You can find the app&amp;rsquo;s settings by following &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/">this step-by-step guide&lt;/a>.&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="creating-templates">Creating templates&lt;/h2>
&lt;figure class="flex flex-col items-center">
 &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/templates-overview.png" target="_blank" class="flex flex-col items-center">
 &lt;img src="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/templates-overview.png" alt="Template management overview"class="max-h-80 max-w-[min(100%,36rem)] !mb-0 !mt-0 !rounded-md"
 >
 &lt;/a>&lt;figcaption>Template management overview&lt;/figcaption>&lt;/figure>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Please refer to the annotated image, and read the following legend:&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;ol>
&lt;li>You can create up to &lt;strong>100 templates&lt;/strong> for your organization, and will see a count in the top panel.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>The first section/table is for custom templates created and managed by your organization. You can create a template by copying a template provided by PageMailer. You will then be able to modify its settings, assign logos, colors, and more.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>This is the list of provided templates which PageMailer comes with. If you would like to request more base templates to be added, please contact us through our &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/support/">support channel&lt;/a>. Alternatively, PageMailer supports an advanced setting allowing you to &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/custom-html/">write your own HTML &amp;amp; CSS&lt;/a> in your custom templates.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Get started by previewing templates and copying them to make them your own. You can copy the same template multiple times and configure it differently.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ol>
&lt;blockquote>
&lt;p>You can preview provided templates and input your own &lt;a href="#configuring-templates">configuration&lt;/a> to see what it would look like with your branding.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Sending an email</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/basic-usage/send-an-email/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/basic-usage/send-an-email/</guid><description>&lt;p>In this guide, we will go over the steps you&amp;rsquo;ll need to take to send the contents of a &lt;strong>Confluence&lt;/strong> page or blog as a branded email.
To ensure that the branding of the email is conform to your company&amp;rsquo;s branding, please head to our
&lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/">settings documentation&lt;/a> to get started.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="open-the-pagemailer-app">Open the PageMailer app&lt;/h2>
&lt;ol>
&lt;li>Head to the &lt;strong>page&lt;/strong> or &lt;strong>blog&lt;/strong> you wish to send via email.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>From the top right corner, find the &amp;ldquo;Send with PageMailer&amp;rdquo; option under &lt;strong>&amp;hellip;&lt;/strong> → &lt;strong>Apps&lt;/strong> → &lt;strong>Send with PageMailer&lt;/strong> as shown here:
&lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/send-an-email.png" target="_blank" class="flex flex-col items-start">
 &lt;img src="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/send-an-email.png" alt="Open PageMailer" title="Open PageMailer"class="max-h-80 max-w-[min(100%,36rem)] !mb-0 !mt-0 !rounded-md"
 >
 &lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;li>A modal should now open with a preview of the email and a form with a couple of configuration options, as seen here:
&lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/send-an-email-2.png" target="_blank" class="flex flex-col items-start">
 &lt;img src="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/send-an-email-2.png" alt="Send with PageMailer modal" title="Send with PageMailer modal"class="max-h-80 max-w-[min(100%,36rem)] !mb-0 !mt-0 !rounded-md"
 >
 &lt;/a>&lt;/li>
&lt;/ol>
&lt;h2 id="configure-the-email">Configure the email&lt;/h2>
&lt;figure class="flex flex-col items-center">
 &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/send-an-email-3.png" target="_blank" class="flex flex-col items-center">
 &lt;img src="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/send-an-email-3.png" alt="Email configuration and preview"class="max-h-80 max-w-[min(100%,36rem)] !mb-0 !mt-0 !rounded-md"
 >
 &lt;/a>&lt;figcaption>Email configuration and preview&lt;/figcaption>&lt;/figure>&lt;p>&lt;strong>Please refer to the annotated image, and read the following legend:&lt;/strong>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Google account</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/basic-usage/google-account/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/basic-usage/google-account/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="introduction">Introduction&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>You can connect a Google Account to send emails from. Please note than &lt;strong>Atlassian&lt;/strong> handles this connection, and &lt;strong>PageMailer&lt;/strong> will not have direct access to your Google account, and you can disconnect it at any point (see &lt;a href="#disconnecting-a-google-account">Disconnecting a Google account&lt;/a>).&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="connecting-a-google-account">Connecting a Google account&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>&lt;em>&lt;strong>Pre-requisite:&lt;/strong> follow the guide to &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/basic-usage/send-an-email/">send an email&lt;/a> to know how to get to this screen.&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>From within the &amp;ldquo;Send with PageMailer&amp;rdquo; modal, you should see a &lt;strong>Connect Google Account&lt;/strong> button.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Custom HTML in templates</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/custom-html/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/custom-html/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;em>To learn about template management, head to the documentation &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/templates/">page dedicated to templates&lt;/a>.&lt;/em>&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="using-custom-html-in-a-template">Using custom HTML in a template&lt;/h2>
&lt;blockquote>
&lt;p>⚠️ This page is an advanced configuration option for PageMailer. You may want to refrain from using it if you are not familiar with HTML &amp;amp; CSS.&lt;/p>&lt;/blockquote>
&lt;p>Within the modal to &lt;strong>Edit&lt;/strong> a template, scroll all the way down, and you will find this option:&lt;/p>
&lt;figure class="flex flex-col items-center">
 &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/custom-html-button.png" target="_blank" class="flex flex-col items-center">
 &lt;img src="https://pagemailer.app/images/docs/custom-html-button.png" alt="Option to enable custom HTML"class="max-h-80 max-w-[min(100%,36rem)] !mb-0 !mt-0 !rounded-md"
 >
 &lt;/a>&lt;figcaption>Option to enable custom HTML&lt;/figcaption>&lt;/figure>&lt;p>Once the option is enabled, you should see the following:&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Confluence tips</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/confluence-tips/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/confluence-tips/</guid><description>&lt;p>A few practical notes to help you get the most out of PageMailer when preparing content in Confluence intended to be sent as an email.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="turn-rich-links-into-regular-links">Turn rich links into regular links&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>When pasting a link into a Confluence page, it will sometimes be turned into a rich link (or &lt;em>inline card&lt;/em> in Atlassian terms). PageMailer will
be able to process most of these links when they are public or when they are links to other Confluence pages and blogs, but other Atlassian links such as
Jira, Trello, StatusPage, etc. are not currently supported (see our &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/roadmap/">roadmap&lt;/a> for future support).&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Supported macros</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/macros/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/macros/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="list-of-supported-confluence-macros">List of supported Confluence macros&lt;/h2>
