&lt;h2 id="list-of-unsupported-confluence-macros">List of unsupported Confluence macros&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>We may eventually add support for some of what is detailed below, and we encourage you to check out our &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/roadmap/">roadmap&lt;/a> and share your
&lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/support/">feedback&lt;/a> to help us prioritize future changes.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Image processing</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/image-processing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/docs/advanced/image-processing/</guid><description>&lt;p>Upon processing Confluence pages to &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/basic-usage/send-an-email">generate an email&lt;/a> or when &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/settings/logos-socials/#logos">uploading logos&lt;/a>,
PageMailer processes images through our &lt;strong>first-party API&lt;/strong>, which is hosted and owned by PageMailer. This API handles:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Compression&lt;/strong> of JPEG, PNG, and GIF files to reduce file size while maintaining quality.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Conversion&lt;/strong> of SVG files to PNG format for consistent rendering across email clients.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;strong>Resizing&lt;/strong> of images that exceed a certain width to ensure optimal display and reducing file size.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>All image processing is performed securely and &lt;strong>in accordance with our &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/privacy/">Privacy Policy&lt;/a>&lt;/strong>. No third-party services are used for these operations, and your data remains within PageMailer&amp;rsquo;s or Atlassian&amp;rsquo;s infrastructure.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Oops! Page not found</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/404.html</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/404.html</guid><description>&lt;div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto text-center">
&lt;p>We couldn’t find the page you were looking for. It might have been moved, renamed, or never existed. Please &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/support/">let us know&lt;/a> or head back to the &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/">homepage&lt;/a> to continue browsing.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;strong>Need help? The &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/docs/">documentation&lt;/a> and our &lt;a href="https://pagemailer.app/support/">community&lt;/a> are great places to start.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;/div></description></item><item><title>PageMailer on the Atlassian Marketplace</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/go/marketplace/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/go/marketplace/</guid><description/></item><item><title>PageMailer QR Codes</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/qr/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/qr/</guid><description/></item><item><title>Pricing</title><link>https://pagemailer.app/pricing/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://pagemailer.app/pricing/</guid><description>&lt;section class="bg-white">
